 The example uses captured decisions and one surviving captured fact. It does not establish a general matching algorithm, interpret arbitrary edits or provide scientific justification. A future measurement adapter can reuse the guarded replace/rebuild/recovery boundary and these sequence assertions while supplying its own continuity and retirement semantics.
+
+## Retirement of a fact-bearing group — 2026-10-19
+
+| Finding | Activities | Identity process/evidence | Transfer to measurements and other overlays |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Zero retrieved output is not proof of physical cleanup | P, M, R | After retiring g01, verify its node/vector, resolution edge, local fact, old evidence and markers are absent. A failed publication is separately withheld by the ledger | Retiring a measurement must remove its obsolete materialization/evidence, not merely hide it from one query path |
+| Index lifetime follows the index key's sharing granularity | P, M, R | Doc01's fact edge disappears, but doc02's surviving fact uses the same relationship-text index entry; the shared entry and endpoint vector must remain. Optional per-edge Triplet entries have distinct keys | Removing one reading must not erase a unit, predicate or shared vocabulary vector still used by other observations; use each representation's actual keys and native cleanup rules |
+| Authoritative retirement differs from a missing required output | D, P, M | The current source deliberately omits g01/r01 and its construction declaration. Healthy reconcile does not reconstruct them from historical recipes or fixture baseline files | A retired observation/claim must not reappear merely because an old creation recipe still exists in a previous revision or recovery snapshot |
+| Empty semantic output still needs an admitted meaning and checked inputs | D, P, M | The captured replacement no longer contains its known fact span; chunk-map validation and surviving-source verification still run when no primary fact is generated | An explicitly empty replacement can be valid after removal, while skipped processing or invalid input must remain a failure rather than masquerade as successful empty extraction |
+
+The same guarded full-document rebuild and explicit forward-recovery mechanism handles this case. These are captured lifecycle results, not scientific support, extraction accuracy, populated-Triplet deletion evidence or universal same-triple foreign-owner compatibility. Reuse the ownership/index-key checklist and presence/absence sequence assertions before adding a new integration.
